winewayland: tray icons go to the desktop's own tray (StatusNotifierItem), and their menus show.

Seen 11-04 (lab 179, Filmora): a program's tray icon made Wine's explorer show its standalone floating tray window
("Shell_TrayWnd", captioned, 150x47), which KWin put in the middle of the screen over the application. Windows puts the
icon in the taskbar's notification area. His call (C177): "I'm fine with showing them in plasma's own tray, but you'll
also need to add them to the tray of other desktops as well".

explorer hands NIM_ADD to the display driver first (pNotifyIcon) and only creates its own icon when the driver returns
-1. winewayland now answers with a StatusNotifierItem over D-Bus, which the trays of Plasma, GNOME (AppIndicator
extension), XFCE, Cinnamon, MATE, LXQt, Budgie, COSMIC and waybar all show:
- one private connection per icon, org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-<n> at /StatusNotifierItem, registered with
  org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher (the form every watcher accepts); libdbus is dlopen'ed (no new dependency);
- icon = the HICON's pixels (IconPixmap, ARGB32 network order; HICON conversion after Sergei Chernyadyev's SNI driver,
  Wine MR 2808), tooltip/title = szTip as UTF-8 (built by hand: libdbus aborts on invalid UTF-8, so not the unix code
  page), NIM_MODIFY emits NewIcon/NewToolTip/NewTitle, NIS_HIDDEN takes the item off the bus as Windows takes it off
  the tray, NIM_DELETE removes it, NIM_SETVERSION is kept;
- clicks reach the application as explorer relays them (systray.c tray_icon_wndproc/notify_owner): Activate =
  WM_LBUTTONDOWN/UP (WM_LBUTTONDBLCLK for a second click within the double-click time), SecondaryActivate = middle,
  ContextMenu = WM_RBUTTONDOWN/UP; then NIN_SELECT / WM_CONTEXTMENU for uVersion > 0, coordinates in wParam for
  NOTIFYICON_VERSION_4 (mapped from the compositor's logical point to the Win32 desktop per output); the cursor is set
  there first, so GetCursorPos gives the application the click point as on Windows;
- NIF_INFO balloons become org.freedesktop.Notifications (title, text, info/warning/error icon or the icon's pixels,
  suppress-sound), with NIN_BALLOONSHOW, NIN_BALLOONUSERCLICK, NIN_BALLOONTIMEOUT and NIN_BALLOONHIDE back;
- icons whose owner window is gone are removed within a second; a restarted watcher gets every item again;
- the connections are serviced by one thread in explorer (dllmain.c starts it in explorer.exe only).
No watcher on the bus (plain GNOME, a bare compositor), no libdbus, or the kill switch: -1, and explorer's floating
window is the way to the icon as before.

Two winewayland fixes the tray menus needed, both measured with lab/agents/sni/traytest (TrackPopupMenu from a hidden
window on WM_CONTEXTMENU, as tray applications do):
- window.c: a popup menu (#32768) whose owner is an unmapped root was a subsurface of that never-mapped owner, so it
  was never seen -- in explorer's floating tray as well (179: menu window present to Win32, nothing on screen; with
  this: on screen). It now gets its own toplevel, without NEUTRON_WL_ORPHAN_TOPLEVEL (the general promotion stays
  opt-in for its ghost-window case, which a menu cannot hit). Kill switch NEUTRON_ORPHAN_MENU=0.
- wayland_keyboard.c/wayland_surface.c: when this process destroys the focused surface, libwayland delivers the leave
  with a NULL surface and the handler returned before releasing keys; with nothing of ours focused afterwards the real
  key-up never reached Wine and wineserver auto-repeated the key forever. A tray menu closed with Escape left Escape
  repeating into the application, which closed every later menu within ~10 ms. The keys are now released where the
  driver destroyed the focused surface, outside its locks. Kill switch NEUTRON_RELEASE_DESTROYED_FOCUS=0.

Not covered: a client cannot place a Wayland toplevel, so the menu appears where the compositor puts it (KWin: the
middle of the screen, with a taskbar entry while open), not at the icon; drawing it at the icon needs the menu over
com.canonical.dbusmenu, i.e. the application's HMENU from its own process. A click outside the menu closes it only
when the focus leaves the application (NEUTRON_DEACT_ENDMENU). Icons already in the floating window when a watcher
appears stay there. NIN_KEYSELECT. X11 sessions keep winex11's XEmbed docking (Plasma's xembedsniproxy and XEmbed trays
show those, and X11 can place the menu at the icon).

Lab (179 + this = lab 179s; desk-c; lab/agents/sni):
- spec host (snihost.py: watcher + notification server on the desk's own bus): registration, Id/Title/ToolTip/Status,
  IconPixmap 32x32 red centre/transparent corner, after NIM_MODIFY NewIcon+NewToolTip+NewTitle and a blue icon;
  v4 clicks (DOWN/UP/NIN_SELECT, DBLCLK on a quick second click, middle, RBUTTON + WM_CONTEXTMENU, anchor 1000,600 ->
  1750,1050 at 175%), legacy clicks without NIN_SELECT/WM_CONTEXTMENU; balloon -> Notify + NIN_BALLOONSHOW, click ->
  NIN_BALLOONUSERCLICK, expiry -> NIN_BALLOONTIMEOUT, NIM_DELETE closes it; hide -> item leaves the bus, show -> back
  with the new icon; watcher restart -> re-registered at once; app killed -> item gone within 1 s; tip with é, ☃ and
  an emoji under LANG=C arrives as valid UTF-8.
- real Plasma 6 (kded6 + plasmashell nested on the lab desk's own bus, lab HOME): the test icon and Filmora 16's own
  icon in Plasma's tray, Plasma's tooltip ("Tray tést ☃ 😀" too), left click -> DOWN/UP/NIN_SELECT, right click ->
  the application's menu on screen (Filmora's: Open Wondershare Filmora / Screen Recorder / Exit), Escape and item
  clicks close it with the right result; no floating window.
- no watcher: explorer's floating window as before, and its right-click menu now on screen (179: invisible).
- kill switches: NEUTRON_SNI=0 -> no item, floating window; NEUTRON_ORPHAN_MENU=0 -> menu invisible again;
  NEUTRON_RELEASE_DESTROYED_FOCUS=0 -> second menu closed after 8 ms (with the fix it stayed open 2/2).
- not run: GNOME + AppIndicator, XFCE, Cinnamon, waybar -- none is installed here or in the podman images.

