+ * License along with this library; if not, write to the Free Software
+ * Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA 02110-1301, USA
+ */
+
+/* NEUTRON sni-tray (2026-11-04, his C177: "show them in plasma's own tray, but you'll also need to add them to the
+ * tray of other desktops as well").
+ *
+ * Windows puts a Shell_NotifyIcon icon in the taskbar's notification area. Wayland has no XEmbed tray, so explorer
+ * fell back to its own floating "Shell_TrayWnd" window (programs/explorer/systray.c), which KWin placed in the middle
+ * of the screen over the application. Every current desktop tray speaks StatusNotifierItem over D-Bus (Plasma, GNOME
+ * with the AppIndicator extension, XFCE, Cinnamon, MATE, LXQt, Budgie, COSMIC, waybar), so each icon becomes an SNI
+ * item there:
+ *
+ *  - explorer hands NIM_ADD to the driver first (pNotifyIcon) and only creates its own icon when the driver returns
+ *    -1. With no StatusNotifierWatcher on the session bus (plain GNOME, a bare compositor), no libdbus, or the kill
+ *    switch, this returns -1 and the floating window remains the way to reach the icon.
+ *  - one private D-Bus connection per icon, registered as org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-<n> at /StatusNotifierItem,
+ *    the form every watcher accepts;
+ *  - the icon is the HICON's pixels (IconPixmap, ARGB32 in network byte order), the tooltip szTip, NIS_HIDDEN takes
+ *    the item off the bus as Windows takes it off the tray;
+ *  - clicks reach the application exactly as explorer relays them (systray.c tray_icon_wndproc / notify_owner):
+ *    WM_xBUTTONDOWN/UP (WM_LBUTTONDBLCLK for a second click within the double-click time), then NIN_SELECT after a
+ *    left button up and WM_CONTEXTMENU after a right button up for uVersion > 0, with the coordinates in wParam for
+ *    NOTIFYICON_VERSION_4. The cursor position is set to the click first, so an application placing its menu with
+ *    GetCursorPos gets the click point (on Windows the pointer is there);
+ *  - balloons (NIF_INFO) go to org.freedesktop.Notifications, with NIN_BALLOONSHOW, NIN_BALLOONUSERCLICK,
+ *    NIN_BALLOONTIMEOUT and NIN_BALLOONHIDE back to the application;
+ *  - icons whose owner window is gone are removed (Windows leaves them until the pointer passes over them);
+ *  - when the watcher restarts (plasmashell restart), every item registers again.
+ *
+ * The application's own context menu (TrackPopupMenu from its hidden window) needs two winewayland fixes that come
+ * with this: window.c shows a popup menu whose owner is an unmapped root as its own toplevel (it was an invisible
+ * subsurface, in explorer's floating tray too), and wayland_keyboard.c releases the keys when the focused surface is
+ * destroyed (a menu closed with Escape left Escape auto-repeating, which closed every later menu at once).
+ *
+ * Not covered: Wayland does not let a client place a toplevel, so the menu appears where the compositor puts it
+ * (KWin: the middle of the screen, with a taskbar entry while it is open), not at the tray; exporting the menu over
+ * com.canonical.dbusmenu so the desktop draws it at the icon would need the application's HMENU from its own process.
+ * A click outside the menu closes it only when the focus leaves the application. Icons already in explorer's floating
+ * window when a watcher appears stay there. Keyboard selection (NIN_KEYSELECT). X11 sessions keep winex11's XEmbed
+ * docking, which places menus at the icon.
+ * Kill switch NEUTRON_SNI=0. */
+
